  <info>
  <link type="guide" xref="accounting"/>
  <link type="seealso" xref="credit_card_statements"/>
  <desc>Record a card processor's fee, or a card refund, between two
  accounts.</desc>
    <credit type="author">
      <name>Reuben Rissler</name>
      <email>pygtk.posting@gmail.com</email>
    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Credit card merchant</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Accounting</gui><gui>Credit card merchant</gui></guiseq>
  records money the card processor takes out of, or puts back into, what it
  pays you: its fees, or a refund to a customer's card.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Amount</gui> and choose the
    <gui>Date</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Double click the account to debit, from the expense accounts on
    the left, such as card processing fees.</p></item>
    <item><p>Double click the account to credit, from the revenue accounts on
    the right.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Post transaction</gui>. Until it can be posted, the
    button says what is missing, for instance <gui>No debit account
    selected</gui>. A parent account cannot be chosen, only the accounts under
    it.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p><gui>Refresh accounts</gui> reloads the account lists after accounts are
  added in <link xref="accounts_configuration"/>.</p>

</page>
